#AUTO 43
#NEEDED 1
# Hardware RNG recon (issue 110n).
#
# The SoC's true-random-number generator lives in the crypto complex
# (0xFE388000). This probe ungates the crypto bus + RNG clocks and releases
# their resets (a read while gated HANGS the AHB), starts a draw, polls the
# START bit until it self-clears (data ready) with a BOUNDED loop so a wrong
# control value can only time out, and reads the eight output words. Run it
# twice: the words should differ run-to-run; all-equal or all-zero means the
# generator is stuck or the start sequence didn't take.
#
# The start sequence is CONFIRMED against TRM Part 2 Chapter 5 (TRNG): set
# rng_enable, then rng_start (self-clears when data is ready), then read the
# eight output words. Register bases confirmed against TRM Part 1 Table 1-1.
# CRU clock/reset writes done in C behind a CALL. See src/019-probe-engine.c
# (rng_probe) for the register-level detail.

CALL rng_probe
